<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 26 September, from 46 BCE to 1983.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">46 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,980 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar dedicates the Temple of Venus Genetrix</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the celebrations of his triumphs, Caesar dedicated a temple to Venus Genetrix, the mythical ancestress of his family, in his new forum. It proclaimed his divine lineage and unrivalled power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1580 CE <span class="tih-ago">446 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Francis Drake returns from his voyage around the world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Golden Hind sailed into Plymouth after nearly three years, laden with Spanish treasure. Drake was the first captain to complete a circumnavigation and was knighted aboard his ship the next April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1687 CE <span class="tih-ago">339 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Venetian shell blows apart the Parthenon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the Venetian siege of the Acropolis, a mortar shell ignited Ottoman gunpowder stored in the Parthenon. The explosion destroyed the temple's centre and killed some 300 people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1905 CE <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Einstein's paper on special relativity is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Annalen der Physik published Einstein's 'On the Electrodynamics of Moving Bodies', which showed that measurements of time and space depend on the observer's motion. It transformed physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1983 CE <span class="tih-ago">43 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stanislav Petrov judges a Soviet missile alert a false alarm</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Duty officer Stanislav Petrov saw satellite warnings of US missile launches and reported them as a malfunction rather than an attack. He was right, and may have averted a nuclear war.</p></div></li></ol>
